omm2. Record move: from \"1\" to \"2\". Then comm2 size=3.\n\nNode v4: edges to v3(v3 now in 2), v5(2). Own comm2: edges v4-v3 (3) + v4-v5(2)=5. No other connections, so no move.\n\nNode v5: edges to v4(2), v0(1), v3(2). Own comm2: edges to v4(2)+v3(2)=4. To comm0: edge to v0=1, gain=1-4 -1*(3-2)= -3-1= -4. No move.\n\nSo total moves: v2 from 1 to 0, v3 from 1 to 2. That yields final communities: v0:0, v1:0, v2:0, v3:2, v4:2, v5:2. This seems plausible.\n\nThird case (a-002): edges: v0-v1:1, v1-v2:1, v2-v3:2, v3-v4:1, v4-v5:2, v5-v0:2, v0-v2:2, v3-v5:2. Same communities.\n\nCompute node v0: edges v1(1), v2(2), v5(2). Own: v0-v1=1. To comm1: v2 weight2, gain=2-1-1*(2-1)=0 -> zero, not >0. To comm2: v5 weight2, gain=2-1-1*(2-1)=0. No.\n\nNode v1: edges to v0(1), v2(1). Own:1. To comm1: v2 weight1, gain=1-1-1*(2-1)= -1. No.\n\nNode v2: edges to v1(1), v3(2), v0(2). Own comm1: v2-v3=2. To comm0: edges to v1(1)+v0(2)=3, gain=3-2-1*(2-1)=0. To comm2: no edges? v2 not connected to v4 or v5? Actually v3-v5, but v2 only to v3. So no. So no move.\n\nNode v3: edges to v2(2), v4(1), v5(2). Own comm1: v3-v2=2. To comm2: edges to v4(1)+v5(2)=3, gain=3-2-1*(2-1)=0. To comm0: no edges. So no move.\n\nNode v4: edges to v3(1), v5(2). Own comm2: edges to v5=2 (v4-v5), also v3? v3 is in comm1, so not. So w_within_A=2. Candidates: comm1: edge to v3=1 => gain=1-2-1*(2-1)= -2. comm0: no edge. No.\n\nNode v5: edges to v0(2), v4(2), v3(2). Own comm2: edges to v4(2) and v3? v3 in comm1, so only v4=2. So w_within_A=2. Candidates: comm0: edge to v0=2 => gain=2-2-1*(2-1)= -1. comm1: edge to v3=2 => gain=2-2-1*(2-1)= -1. No.\n\nThus no moves. Output communities unchanged, moves empty. That seems fine.\n\nOur implementation produces moves for first two cases and none for third. That is plausible.\n\nNow, we need to write Python code with solve(case). The case argument is the payload dictionary. It contains edges, communities, resolution, _case_nonce. We'll ignore _case_nonce. We need to ensure we